{{!
    @template local_embeddiscussion/preview

    An embedded discussion, or the dashboard, as the editor shows it: a header naming it, over its
    skeleton. Never live in the editor, for anyone - there is nothing to click inside it but the
    whole, which opens the discussion's settings for a teacher who may change them.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * dashboard (bool) The course dashboard rather than a discussion.
    * name (string) The discussion's name, formatted.
    * anonymous (bool) Whether the discussion is anonymous.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "dashboard": false,
        "name": "Week 1 questions",
        "anonymous": true
    }
}}
<div class="embeddisc-preview{{#dashboard}} embeddisc-preview-dashboard{{/dashboard}}">
  <div class="embeddisc-preview-header">
    <span class="embeddisc-preview-icon" aria-hidden="true">{{#pix}}t/messages, core{{/pix}}</span>
    <span class="embeddisc-preview-title">
      {{#dashboard}}{{#str}}dashboard, local_embeddiscussion{{/str}}{{/dashboard}}
      {{^dashboard}}{{#str}}previewtitle, local_embeddiscussion, {{name}}{{/str}}{{/dashboard}}
    </span>
    {{#anonymous}}<span class="badge badge-secondary embeddisc-preview-badge">{{#str}}anonymous, local_embeddiscussion{{/str}}</span>{{/anonymous}}
  </div>
  {{#dashboard}}{{> local_embeddiscussion/dashboard_skeleton }}{{/dashboard}}
  {{^dashboard}}{{> local_embeddiscussion/skeleton }}{{/dashboard}}
</div>
